  "pages": {
    "welcoming": {
      "title": "Welcome to Pizzeria Forcella",
      "content": {
        "highlights": [
          "Neapolitan pizza originated in Naples, Italy, and over time it became one of the most famous symbols of traditional Italian cuisine. Its history dates back centuries and reflects the simplicity and authenticity of local cooking traditions. Today it is recognized around the world as a cultural and culinary icon of Italy.",
          "It is prepared using carefully selected ingredients such as San Marzano tomatoes, fresh mozzarella, extra virgin olive oil, and aromatic basil. Each ingredient plays an important role in creating the balanced and authentic flavor of the pizza. The focus is always on freshness, quality, and respecting traditional preparation methods.",
          "The pizza is baked in a traditional wood-fired oven at extremely high temperatures, often exceeding 450°C. This intense heat cooks the pizza in about 60–90 seconds, allowing the dough to rise quickly and develop its characteristic soft and airy texture. The result is a light crust with slightly charred edges and a delicate smoky flavor."
        ]
      }
    },

